"""
Users, login and logout over server-side sessions in SQLite.

A user is a name and an Argon2id hash of the password (Standard.Password);
the password itself is never stored and never logged.  A name is 1 to 64
bytes of lowercase letters, digits, dot, hyphen and underscore.  A
password follows the rules of Wolly.Passphrase (NIST SP 800-63B-4) when it
is set, and is brought to NFKC before it is hashed and before it is
checked at a login.  A login refuses a password shorter than the shortest
any user may have, or longer than Wolly.Passphrase.mostBytes, before it is
hashed, so a request cannot make the server hash a megabyte.

A session is Standard.Session's: its token goes to the browser in the
cookie named by cookieName, with Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict and
Path=/, and the database keeps only its digest.  A visitor gets a session
before the login, for the token of the form against forgery; the login gives the
session a new token, so a token set by someone else before the login
opens nothing after it; the logout removes the session on the server.

A client, the address the web server names, that failed failureLimit
times within failureWindowSeconds is refused without its password being
looked at, and so is a user name that failed as often from any number of
clients.  The second limit lets anyone who knows a name keep its user out
for the window; it is the price of stopping many addresses from trying
one name.  A login clears the failures of its client and of its name.  A name that does not exist costs the same hash as one that
does, so the time of an answer does not tell whether a name is taken.

A user who turned on the second factor of Wolly.Totp is not logged in by
the password alone: login then answers CodeNeeded, and the session holds
the user as waiting for a code, which sessionUser does not count as
logged in.  loginCode takes the code within pendingSeconds of the
password and logs the user in under yet another token.  A wrong code is a
failure of the client and of the name, as a wrong password is, and the
right password does not clear the failures of such a user: only the
right code does, so knowing the password does not buy more tries at the
code.

Every login, failure, refusal and logout is a line of JSON in the audit
log the caller names: the event, the user name, the client and the
outcome, never a password or a token.
"""
import Standard.String (
    String
);
import Standard.Database (
    Database,
    Writing,
    DbError
);
import Standard.FcgiServer (
    Request
);
import Wolly.Response (
    Response
);

module Wolly.Auth is
    """
    Why a call did not do its work.
    """
    union AuthError: Free is
        """
        SQLite refused a statement.
        """
        case AuthStorage is
            error: DbError;
        """
        The random source, the digest or the password hash failed.
        """
        case AuthCrypto;
        """
        A time below 0 was passed.
        """
        case AuthBadTime;
    end;

    """
    What a login came to.  Linear: LoggedIn carries the new token.
    """
    union LoginResult: Linear is
        """
        The name and the password fit.  token is the new token of the
        session, for the cookie.
        """
        case LoggedIn is
            token: String;
        """
        The name and the password fit, and the user has the second factor
        on.  token is the new token of the session, which waits for the
        code: loginCode takes it.
        """
        case CodeNeeded is
            token: String;
        """
        The name or the password did not fit, or the name is no name.
        """
        case Refused;
        """
        The client failed too often of late; nothing was checked.
        """
        case Throttled;
        """
        The work could not be done.
        """
        case LoginFailed is
            error: AuthError;
    end;

    """
    How many failures within failureWindowSeconds throttle a client, and
    as many a user name: 5.
    """
    function failureLimit(): Int64
        ensures result = 5;

    """
    The time over which failures are counted: 900 seconds.
    """
    function failureWindowSeconds(): Int64
        ensures result = 900;

    """
    The name of the session cookie.
    """
    function cookieName(): Span[Nat8, Static]
        ensures spanLength(result) > 0;

    """
    How long a session waits for the code after the password: 300 seconds.
    """
    function pendingSeconds(): Int64
        ensures result = 300;

    """
    Makes the tables of users, of failures by client and by name, of the
    seeds of Wolly.Totp and of sessions when the database has none.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function prepareAuth(db: &![Database[Writing], R]): Either[AuthError, Unit];

    """
    Whether name is a user name: 1 to 64 bytes of a to z, 0 to 9, dot,
    hyphen and underscore.
    No contract: a walk over name.
    """
    generic [N: Region]
    function isUserName(name: Span[Nat8, N]): Bool;

    """
    Adds the user name with the hash of password in NFKC.  Right false
    when name is no user name, the name is taken, or the password does not
    fit the rules of Wolly.Passphrase for a user without a second factor,
    with the list of known passwords at listPath.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region, N: Region, P: Region, L: Region]
    function addUser(db: &![Database[Writing], R], name: Span[Nat8, N], password: Span[Nat8, P],
                     listPath: Span[Nat8, L]): Either[AuthError, Bool];

    """
    Changes the password of name from current to next.  Right false when
    current is not the password of name, or next does not fit the rules of
    Wolly.Passphrase: with a second factor on, 8 characters are enough.
    The sessions of name stay.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region, N: Region, C: Region, P: Region, L: Region]
    function changePassword(db: &![Database[Writing], R], name: Span[Nat8, N], current: Span[Nat8, C],
                            next: Span[Nat8, P], listPath: Span[Nat8, L]): Either[AuthError, Bool];

    """
    A new session for a visitor who is not logged in, made at now.  Right
    holds its token.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function startSession(db: &![Database[Writing], R], now: Int64): Either[AuthError, String]
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    The token of a live session for a visitor at now: token itself when
    it opens a session that is within its limits, else the token of a new
    one, so that a page asked for again does not make a session each time.
    """
    generic [R: Region, T: Region]
    function visitorSession(db: &![Database[Writing], R], token: Span[Nat8, T], now: Int64): Either[AuthError, String]
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    The login of name with password from client at now, in the session
    of token, which may be empty or no session at all.  Writes a line to
    the audit log at auditPath.
    """
    generic [R: Region, T: Region, N: Region, P: Region, C: Region, A: Region]
    function login(db: &![Database[Writing], R], token: Span[Nat8, T], name: Span[Nat8, N],
                   password: Span[Nat8, P], client: Span[Nat8, C], now: Int64, auditPath: Span[Nat8, A]): LoginResult
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    The code of the second factor from client at now, in the session of
    token that login left waiting for it.  The seed opens under key.
    LoggedIn with a new token when the code fits; Refused when it does
    not, when token opens no waiting session, or when the session waited
    longer than pendingSeconds; Throttled as login is.  Writes a line to
    the audit log at auditPath.
    """
    generic [R: Region, K: Region, T: Region, C: Region, D: Region, A: Region]
    function loginCode(db: &![Database[Writing], R], key: Span[Nat8, K], token: Span[Nat8, T], code: Span[Nat8, C],
                       client: Span[Nat8, D], now: Int64, auditPath: Span[Nat8, A]): LoginResult
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    Removes the user name and the failures counted for it.  Right true when
    there was such a user.  A session of name opens nothing afterwards,
    since sessionUser asks whether the user is there.  What other modules
    keep of name (roles, passkeys, the second factor, tokens) is theirs to
    remove; examples/login removes it all with login deluser.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region, N: Region]
    function removeUser(db: &![Database[Writing], R], name: Span[Nat8, N]): Either[AuthError, Bool];

    """
    Whether password is the one of name, asked again before a change that
    must not follow from a session alone, such as a new passkey.  Counts as
    login does: a wrong password is a failure of client and of name, and
    Right false comes without a check once either is throttled.
    """
    generic [R: Region, N: Region, P: Region, C: Region]
    function confirmPassword(db: &![Database[Writing], R], name: Span[Nat8, N], password: Span[Nat8, P],
                             client: Span[Nat8, C], now: Int64): Either[AuthError, Bool]
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    The login with a passkey from client at now, in the session of token:
    Wolly.Passkey.authenticate checks the credential, the client data, the
    authenticator data and the signature, and only when it passes is the
    session given to the user of the credential, under a new token.  There
    is no login without a check here: the check is this function's.  A
    second factor is not asked, since a passkey that verified the user is
    one already.  A refusal counts as a failure of client, as a wrong
    password does, and Throttled comes as for login; a name is not
    throttled, since it is known only after the check.  Writes a line to
    the audit log at auditPath.
    """
    generic [R: Region, T: Region, D: Region, X: Region, U: Region, S: Region, I: Region, O: Region, C: Region, A: Region]
    function passkeyLogin(db: &![Database[Writing], R], token: Span[Nat8, T], credential: Span[Nat8, D],
                          clientData: Span[Nat8, X], authenticatorData: Span[Nat8, U], signature: Span[Nat8, S],
                          rpId: Span[Nat8, I], origin: Span[Nat8, O], client: Span[Nat8, C], now: Int64,
                          auditPath: Span[Nat8, A]): LoginResult
        requires now > 0;

    """
    Writes one line of the audit log at auditPath: the event, the user (-
    when it is no user name), the client and the outcome.  The line is
    written only under a writing transaction of db, so that it waits while
    Wolly.AuditLog rewrites the log and lands in the new one: when the busy
    time of the database passes, begin is tried again until it holds, and
    the line carries lock_retries, the number of tries that failed.  False
    when the log could not be written, or begin failed otherwise than busy;
    the line is then lost, never written without the lock.
    No contract: the outcome is the result of I/O.
    """
    generic [R: Region, A: Region, U: Region, C: Region]
    function audit(db: &![Database[Writing], R], auditPath: Span[Nat8, A], event: Span[Nat8, Static], user: Span[Nat8, U],
                   client: Span[Nat8, C], outcome: Span[Nat8, Static]): Bool;

    """
    Logs name in for a sign-in another service vouched for, such as RAMBO
    after Wolly.Rambo checked its ID token: no password, no code and no
    count of failures here, the service did that.  The session of token
    goes on under a new token, or a new one is made, holding the user, as
    after login.  Right Some the new token; Right None when name is no
    user of this application, which keeps who may do what.  The outcome
    goes to the audit log at auditPath (event login-external).
    """
    generic [R: Region, T: Region, N: Region, A: Region, C: Region]
    function externalLogin(db: &![Database[Writing], R], token: Span[Nat8, T], name: Span[Nat8, N], auditPath: Span[Nat8, A],
                           client: Span[Nat8, C], now: Int64): Either[AuthError, Option[String]]
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    The user of the session of token at now: Right None when there is no
    such session, it is over its limits, or nobody logged in with it.
    """
    generic [R: Region, T: Region]
    function sessionUser(db: &![Database[Writing], R], token: Span[Nat8, T], now: Int64): Either[AuthError, Option[String]]
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    Ends the session of token on the server and writes a line to the
    audit log at auditPath.  A token that opens nothing is no failure.
    """
    generic [R: Region, T: Region, C: Region, A: Region]
    function logout(db: &![Database[Writing], R], token: Span[Nat8, T], client: Span[Nat8, C], now: Int64,
                    auditPath: Span[Nat8, A]): Either[AuthError, Unit]
        requires now >= 0;

    """
    The session token the request carries in its cookie, when it has the
    form of one.
    No contract: an Option read from the request.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function sessionToken(request: &[Request, R]): Option[String];

    """
    The response with the Set-Cookie header that gives the browser token.
    No contract: what the opaque response holds is not stated in O(1).
    """
    generic [T: Region]
    function withSessionCookie(response: Response, token: Span[Nat8, T]): Response;

    """
    The response with the Set-Cookie header that removes the cookie.
    No contract: what the opaque response holds is not stated in O(1).
    """
    function withoutSessionCookie(response: Response): Response;
end module.
